OL,3,GNEWSA'The wood is alive': Ranger
OL,4,Aretires after 38 years
OL,5,
OL,6,FA "passionate" woodsman who spent
OL,7,Falmost four decades caring for wildlife
OL,8,Fhas retired.
OL,10,FWilliam McLaughlin spent 37 years
OL,11,Fworking as Forestry England wildlife
OL,12,Franger at Bourne Woods, in
OL,13,FLincolnshire.
OL,15,FThe 68-year-old, who was responsible
OL,16,Ffor conservation and deer management,
OL,17,Fsaid: "If your job is your hobby, you
OL,18,Fdon't work a day in your life."
